From 0dc98d9e6131d3dc469e5c5f1febb66f9020b88f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:20:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Rollback hooks: frame boundary hook, machine
 snapshot/restore, state hash, pad input provider

- EeScheduler: boundary hook at the top of the dispatcher (every VBlankStart, or a main-thread wake),
  SavedState save/load of every guest-visible scheduler member, a deterministic state digest; with a hook
  installed, cycle-due events fire in EE-cycle order and the timer-vs-vblank wait compares cycles, not host
  times (host pacing can no longer reorder events). No hook: unchanged behaviour.
- PS2Memory: PS2DeviceState save/load (I/O regs, GS privileged regs, VIF0/1, DMA, PATH2/3 cut state,
  pending transfers, DMAC causes, EE timers, MFIFO).
- ps2_rollback: capture/restore of RDRAM, scratchpad, VU memories, scheduler, devices, VU0/VU1
  interpreters, guest heap bookkeeping, pad ports; masked per-page RDRAM hash + full-state hash.
- Pad stub: PadInputProvider (frame-exact scripted / rollback input), savePadState/loadPadState.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
